UNUserNotificationCenter: a tap on a notification reaches the delegate's didReceive as the default action, as on iOS. The notification's intent carries its request identifier, post time and a one-time token the worker records; UIApplication.launch reads the tap that started the activity and listens for later ones; only an intent presenting the identifier's current token counts (the activity is exported), the tap spends it, so a recreated activity's launch intent is not delivered twice; a malformed intent is ignored; a tap waits for a delegate when there is none yet. Proposed upstream.

